<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="017" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>B-2 one decision result mapper</title>
    <phase>A BFF rework</phase>
    <gate>after 011 (done)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api; modifies 3 endpoint .cs files and adds a new mapper</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Cross-cutting refactor of 3 endpoint files on the public REST contract (byte-for-byte) plus a new shared abstraction (one reasonCode vocabulary for REST and MCP)</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Shares no file with 001 (spike worktree) or 011 (done, test files only); serial with 013 through deps</parallel-reason>
    <deps>011</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, api, refactoring, unit-test, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Extract the result-to-HTTP mapping from the Signals endpoint statics into one DecisionResultMapper that maps SignalReadResult and DecisionCommitResult (and the plan results) to ProblemDetails for REST or to a transport-neutral tool error for MCP, with one reasonCode vocabulary and REST responses byte-for-byte unchanged.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in ASP.NET Core ProblemDetails and API contract preservation.</role>
  <goal>Api/Signals/DecisionResultMapper.cs is the only place the decision slice maps results; the three endpoint files call it; 011's baselines pass unchanged; every reason code REST can return has an MCP mapping unit test.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Design §8 B-2: mapping lives in endpoint statics (DecisionCommitEndpoints.cs:60-118, SignalReadEndpoints.cs:46-83, DecisionPlanEndpoints.cs:251-345); a second host would fork it. Spec FR-09. The MCP SDK arrives in 020, so the MCP side is a transport-neutral DecisionToolError(ReasonCode, Message, Status) that Api/Mcp converts to CallToolResult (020's McpToolResults).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Signals/DecisionResultMapper.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Signals/DecisionCommitEndpoints.cs (ToHttp L61, L93; statics L60-118)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Signals/SignalReadEndpoints.cs (L46-83, L85)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Signals/DecisionPlanEndpoints.cs (AccessUnavailable L138, CallerUnresolved L149, L251-345)</file>
      <file role="new">tests/unit/domain/Signals/DecisionResultMapperTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/contract-baseline.md (reason-code inventory from 011)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionCommitService.cs (DecisionCommitReasons L199-245)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="011" status="complete">Golden baselines and the reason-code inventory</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">The REST responses of GET /api/v1/signals/worklist, GET /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision-plan, GET /api/v1/signals/{id}/suppression and POST /api/v1/signals/{id}/decision stay byte-for-byte unchanged: task 011's contract baseline tests pass with no golden-file edit (FR-09).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">The mapper reuses the existing reason-code constants unchanged (no renaming, no new code in this task); REST output keeps the exact ProblemDetails type, title, status, detail and extension members the statics produce today.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Domain failures never become transport errors: the MCP side of the mapper always yields an isError tool result carrying reasonCode and a message that says how to fix the call (FR-09).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">MCP error messages contain no record text, party names or matter names; they name the reason and the fix only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Finance's errorCode vocabulary is out of scope; record the drift in notes, do not change Finance.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Every PR from this task that touches Services/Signals/**, Api/Signals/** or the worklist route is reviewed by spaarke-ontology-platform-r1 before merge (project CLAUDE.md §4); run /conflict-check before opening it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source text: spec.md 'Placement Justification'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': a delta of +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, a total of 55 MB or more triggers architecture review, and the total must stay at or under 60 MB (hard stop). No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/error-handling.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/pre-pipeline-context.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read the three endpoint files' mapping statics and 011's reason-code inventory.</step>
    <step order="2">Create DecisionResultMapper with ToHttp(...) for each result type (behaviour copied verbatim from the statics) and ToToolError(...) returning DecisionToolError(ReasonCode, Message, Status) for every non-success result.</step>
    <step order="3">Replace the statics in the three endpoints with mapper calls; delete the duplicated code.</step>
    <step order="4">Write DecisionResultMapperTests: one case per reason code in the inventory (isError true, reasonCode identical, non-empty fix message), including decided_in_invoice_review → 'decide in Invoice Review'; unknown code; success.</step>
    <step order="5">Run 011's baselines and the Signals suites; measure the publish-size delta; open the PR for ontology review.</step>
    <step order="6">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="7">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r1/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If any 011 baseline differs by even one byte, STOP and escalate rather than editing the golden file (AP-9).</trigger>
    <trigger>If a reason code exists in code but cannot be produced by any route, record it in notes and escalate only if it affects the MCP mapping test set.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Endpoint statics DecisionCommitEndpoints.cs:60-118 (ToHttp L61), SignalReadEndpoints.cs:46-83, DecisionPlanEndpoints.cs:251-345.</existing>
    <extension>Yes, it extends them: the statics are moved into one mapper and the endpoints call it; nothing new is invented beyond the MCP-side tool error.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>MCP results would map reason codes separately and drift from REST (Finance already drifted: errorCode vs reasonCode), so the widget and model would see different failures than the Console.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build and test .NET projects (dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test)</tool>
    <tool name="terminal">Run shell commands</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Signals/DecisionResultMapper.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/domain/Signals/DecisionResultMapperTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">011's contract baselines pass with zero golden-file changes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Each reason code in notes/contract-baseline.md has a unit test asserting its MCP mapping: isError true, the identical reasonCode, a non-empty message that says how to fix the call; decided_in_invoice_review's message points to Invoice Review.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an unknown reason code maps to an isError result that passes the code through, not an exception; a success result never maps to an error.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The three endpoint files contain no mapping statics; no reason-code string literal exists outside the constants and the mapper (grep evidence).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records the publish-size delta (at or under 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE) and the ontology review.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>The mapper needs no caller context (spec FR-10 as amended 2026-11-07, option C), so it no longer waits for the cancelled 012. DecisionToolError is a plain record in Api/Signals; 020 adds Api/Mcp/McpToolResults.cs to convert it to the SDK's CallToolResult so tool tasks 022–024 share one conversion.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
